1
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,679
Well, if it isn't Nancheng's very own

2
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:57,600
Property Tycoon, Mr. Ma?

3
00:00:58,119 --> 00:00:58,759
Mr. Ma!

4
00:00:59,119 --> 00:01:00,840
Here for your demolition payout today?

5
00:01:02,799 --> 00:01:03,759
Oh, it's you.

6
00:01:03,759 --> 00:01:04,319
Yes, that's me!

7
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:05,040
So,

8
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:06,040
got some big business today?

9
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:09,879
Aren't you the big business?

10
00:01:10,079 --> 00:01:11,719
For those 14 properties of yours,

11
00:01:11,719 --> 00:01:12,760
how much did you get?

12
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:14,239
Why do you ask?

13
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:16,959
Now that you've made such a fortune,

14
00:01:17,519 --> 00:01:18,840
could you use someone

15
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:20,159
to serve tea,

16
00:01:20,519 --> 00:01:22,519
cook, clean, and take care of you?

17
00:01:28,959 --> 00:01:30,000
Mr. Ma!

18
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,480
Do you know why I became a realtor?

19
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:33,400
I don't really care to know.

20
00:01:34,439 --> 00:01:35,879
When I was little, a fortune teller...

21
00:01:35,879 --> 00:01:37,159
...told me that in the future,

22
00:01:37,159 --> 00:01:39,560
I'd marry a real estate tycoon.

23
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,760
Then I hope your dream comes true.

24
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:44,319
Wait, you don't get what I mean!

25
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:45,799
May your dream come true.

26
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:47,319
Xiaomei.

27
00:01:47,719 --> 00:01:49,480
Still haven't managed to sell yourself?

28
00:01:50,959 --> 00:01:52,079
Hey, I'm almost there.

29
00:01:52,439 --> 00:01:53,159
Mr. Ma!

30
00:01:53,599 --> 00:01:54,359
Mr. Ma!

31
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,120
You're finally here!

32
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:56,959
Right this way, honored guest.

33
00:01:58,400 --> 00:01:58,959
Mr. Ma!

34
00:01:59,439 --> 00:02:01,120
Just a few more words! Let's chat!

35
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,439
Mr. Ma!

36
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:10,879
If only I'd treated him better back then.

37
00:02:11,199 --> 00:02:11,879
Otherwise, right now...

38
00:02:11,879 --> 00:02:13,360
...I'd be a multi-millionaire's wife.

39
00:02:14,719 --> 00:02:16,280
I'm such a damn fool!

40
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:18,280
Doing the laundry?

41
00:02:18,439 --> 00:02:19,080
Dawei!

42
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,560
I have another dish almost ready.

43
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:21,560
Go ahead and eat with Dad first.

44
00:02:22,639 --> 00:02:23,479
Ones,

45
00:02:23,599 --> 00:02:24,479
tens,

46
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:25,599
hundreds,

47
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:26,560
thousands,

48
00:02:27,199 --> 00:02:27,879
ten thousands,

49
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,199
hundred thousands,

50
00:02:30,479 --> 00:02:31,199
millions...

51
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:33,120
Seven million!

52
00:02:34,199 --> 00:02:35,039
Oh my god!

53
00:02:35,879 --> 00:02:36,879
In all my life,

54
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,039
I haven't even seen 70,000!

55
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:40,960
Dawei...

56
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,800
This money...

57
00:02:43,879 --> 00:02:45,080
Is it really all ours?

58
00:02:45,319 --> 00:02:46,199
It's all ours.

59
00:02:46,759 --> 00:02:47,719
Every single penny.

60
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:48,840
Completely clean and legit.

61
00:02:51,159 --> 00:02:52,719
As for Sister Yi's money,

62
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:55,759
she'll put it all in the garment factory.

63
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:58,159
She'll only make more when the time comes.

64
00:03:03,199 --> 00:03:03,960
Great!

65
00:03:05,159 --> 00:03:05,639
Here you go again!

66
00:03:06,639 --> 00:03:07,800
You promised not to hit me!

67
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:12,840
Okay...

68
00:03:13,479 --> 00:03:14,400
You little rascal.

69
00:03:15,199 --> 00:03:17,639
Seeing you loafing around back then,

70
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,719
looking like a good-for-nothing,

71
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:22,960
I wanted to whip you with my belt.

72
00:03:23,479 --> 00:03:24,319
Actually...

73
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,240
Dad was just furious at himself.

74
00:03:27,439 --> 00:03:29,479
I was useless and couldn't protect you two.

75
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,840
If your big brother were still alive...

76
00:03:39,479 --> 00:03:40,240
Today's a happy day.

77
00:03:40,639 --> 00:03:41,520
Let's not bring this up.

78
00:03:41,919 --> 00:03:42,719
No more sad talk.

79
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:45,840
Let's eat.

80
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:46,680
Mom passed away early,

81
00:03:46,919 --> 00:03:48,719
and Dad's health kept deteriorating.

82
00:03:48,879 --> 00:03:50,400
To earn money, Big Brother...

83
00:03:50,639 --> 00:03:51,759
...overloaded his cargo truck,

84
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,439
and ended up in a fatal crash,

85
00:03:54,199 --> 00:03:56,080
leaving behind a debt of 200,000.

86
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:59,240
That debt pushed our family over the edge.

87
00:04:00,439 --> 00:04:01,400
In my past life,

88
00:04:01,719 --> 00:04:03,319
I failed everyone and ended up in prison.

89
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,560
Dad shouldered all the debts alone,

90
00:04:07,199 --> 00:04:08,560
slaved away at construction sites,

91
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:11,400
and was worked to death in the end.

92
00:04:12,759 --> 00:04:13,680
In this life,

93
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,960
I've finally kept you by my side.

94
00:04:17,279 --> 00:04:17,879
Dad.

95
00:04:19,639 --> 00:04:20,720
If Mom and Big Brother...

96
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,560
...looked down from heaven

97
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,000
and saw our family standing tall and proud,

98
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:26,600
they'd definitely be thrilled.

99
00:04:30,839 --> 00:04:32,279
I was a bastard back then.

100
00:04:32,879 --> 00:04:33,519
I deserved every beating.

101
00:04:34,759 --> 00:04:35,480
From now on,

102
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:38,040
I will be the one you can lean on.

103
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,600
To me,

104
00:04:44,439 --> 00:04:46,360
no amount of money in this bankbook

105
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:49,040
can beat having you sitting right here,

106
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:51,319
sharing a happy drink, father and son.

107
00:04:57,959 --> 00:04:59,560
Live a long life, Dad,

108
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:01,600
and watch me closely.

109
00:05:02,759 --> 00:05:03,959
Everything I owed you before,

110
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:06,000
and owed this family,

111
00:05:07,079 --> 00:05:09,759
I'll make it up a thousandfold.

112
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:14,920
I'll make you Nancheng's proudest man.

113
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:15,800
You... you just...

114
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,480
Stop trying to sweet-talk me!

115
00:05:17,839 --> 00:05:20,000
Back when I whacked you with my shoe,

116
00:05:20,279 --> 00:05:22,079
I couldn't beat a squeak out of you.

117
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:24,000
How'd you get so talkative now?

118
00:05:24,639 --> 00:05:25,639
Who'd you learn that from?

119
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:27,560
I definitely got that from Mom.

120
00:05:28,279 --> 00:05:29,040
Dumplings are ready!

121
00:05:29,959 --> 00:05:30,560
What are you talking about?

122
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:31,360
Nothing.

123
00:05:31,519 --> 00:05:32,480
Why aren't you digging in?

124
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:33,199
Try this.

125
00:05:35,639 --> 00:05:36,120
Here.

126
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:38,720
This little bit of money is nothing.

127
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:42,360
I, Ma Dawei, will make some real waves,

128
00:05:42,639 --> 00:05:44,040
and rake in a real fortune!

129
00:05:44,959 --> 00:05:46,480
I'll make sure our Ma family

130
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:48,480
lives a life everyone in Nancheng envies,

131
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,879
living right at the top!

132
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:54,519
Oh, right.

133
00:05:56,079 --> 00:05:56,879
Dad, Sister-in-law,

134
00:05:58,879 --> 00:06:00,279
I picked out a new house the other day.

135
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:02,000
We're moving soon.

136
00:06:02,079 --> 00:06:02,800
Go have a look at it too.

137
00:06:03,199 --> 00:06:04,639
We're getting a brand-new home!

138
00:06:05,439 --> 00:06:06,040
Money comes and goes—

139
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,279
earn what you can, spend what you want.

140
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:10,720
Come on, Dad.

141
00:06:10,839 --> 00:06:11,839
Let's have a drink together.

142
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:12,240
Alright.

143
00:06:12,879 --> 00:06:13,439
Come on, cheers.

144
00:06:14,319 --> 00:06:14,839
Cheers!

145
00:06:20,759 --> 00:06:21,959
Hello, here's the computer you ordered,

146
00:06:21,959 --> 00:06:23,240
along with this bulky monitor.

147
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,000
Where should I put it?

148
00:06:24,279 --> 00:06:24,879
Sir,

149
00:06:25,399 --> 00:06:26,639
just put it on the desk in my room.

150
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:27,800
Careful, don't bump it.

151
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:29,680
It's so big!

152
00:06:30,199 --> 00:06:31,279
Doesn't look cheap at all.

153
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:32,360
Dad,

154
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:33,639
didn't you hear Dawei?

155
00:06:33,639 --> 00:06:34,519
It's called a computer.

156
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:35,519
It costs a fortune!

157
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,120
One costs several thousand,

158
00:06:37,199 --> 00:06:38,160
some even over ten grand.

159
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:40,160
That expensive?

160
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:42,600
Then...

161
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:44,519
what did he buy that thing for?

162
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,000
You can't eat it or drink it.

163
00:06:46,319 --> 00:06:47,600
Isn't that just throwing money away?

164
00:06:49,279 --> 00:06:50,439
It's stressing me out!

165
00:06:52,279 --> 00:06:53,959
The old folks were totally right.

166
00:06:54,399 --> 00:06:56,240
The sudden rich can't hold on to wealth.

167
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:58,279
Back then, he was flat broke.

168
00:06:58,399 --> 00:06:59,800
Now with millions in his pocket,

169
00:07:00,319 --> 00:07:01,720
he's getting way too cocky!

170
00:07:04,319 --> 00:07:05,120
Don't worry, Dad.

171
00:07:05,279 --> 00:07:06,480
It's not a toy.

172
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:07,839
It's an investment tool.

173
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:09,199
Trust me,

174
00:07:09,519 --> 00:07:10,319
this hunk of metal

175
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,920
will earn our family a mountain of gold.

176
00:07:13,439 --> 00:07:14,160
What mountain?

177
00:07:14,439 --> 00:07:15,319
Brother Dawei!

178
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:17,959
What brings you here?

179
00:07:18,079 --> 00:07:18,959
Sister-in-law, Uncle.

180
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:22,439
What's this?

181
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:25,399
No idea what my dad was thinking.

182
00:07:25,759 --> 00:07:26,399
He said

183
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:28,560
the 51% absolute controlling stake

184
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:29,399
will be handed over to you.

185
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:30,480
From now on,

186
00:07:30,839 --> 00:07:32,480
you're the real boss of Jinhua.

187
00:07:35,319 --> 00:07:35,879
Dawei is the boss?

188
00:07:35,879 --> 00:07:38,360
My dad and I answer to you now, Mr. Ma!

189
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,759
Uncle Dong really broadened his horizons!

190
00:07:41,079 --> 00:07:41,519
Alright,

191
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:42,560
I'll accept this for now.

192
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,439
Soon enough, I'll show you

193
00:07:44,439 --> 00:07:46,600
what real capital leverage looks like.

194
00:07:48,319 --> 00:07:49,120
What did he say?

195
00:07:49,319 --> 00:07:50,360
What leverage?

196
00:07:50,639 --> 00:07:51,560
I don't get it either.

197
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:53,680
Does that mean making lots of money?

198
00:07:56,079 --> 00:07:57,160
Is that for real?

199
00:07:58,480 --> 00:08:00,720
The seed capital is finally secured.

200
00:08:01,759 --> 00:08:02,480
What comes next

201
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,480
is exponential growth.

202
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,360
In prison during my previous life,

203
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:09,839
my only daily pastime

204
00:08:09,839 --> 00:08:11,839
was watching the financial channel

205
00:08:11,959 --> 00:08:13,000
and stock market news.

206
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,399
The trends of those monster stocks

207
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:17,079
and high-flying stocks, I know by heart.

208
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:19,680
Now it will all pay off!

209
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,399
Ma Dawei!

210
00:08:26,079 --> 00:08:27,560
I called you for dinner but no answer!

211
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,519
The food is getting cold.

212
00:08:29,199 --> 00:08:29,839
Sister-in-law!

213
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,360
You came at just the right time.

214
00:08:31,959 --> 00:08:32,679
Come take a look!

215
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:33,559
Look at what?

216
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:37,200
What is all this?

217
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:38,919
Red and green lines, looking like an ECG.

218
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,399
What game are you playing?

219
00:08:40,639 --> 00:08:41,600
These are stocks.

220
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,480
It's not a game!

221
00:08:42,639 --> 00:08:43,240
Look.

222
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,919
Red means it went up,

223
00:08:45,039 --> 00:08:45,679
which means making money.

224
00:08:45,799 --> 00:08:47,200
Green means it went down,

225
00:08:47,399 --> 00:08:48,120
which means losing money.

226
00:08:48,759 --> 00:08:50,000
Red is profit,

227
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,159
and green is loss?

228
00:08:51,759 --> 00:08:54,039
Then your screen is completely red.

229
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:56,360
These ones called Shen Development

230
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:57,360
and Sichuan Changhong...

231
00:08:57,639 --> 00:08:58,759
Why did the numbers stop moving?

232
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,759
Because they hit the Limit up!

233
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:01,759
Sister-in-law,

234
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:03,440
in the time it took you to cook,

235
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:05,799
the stocks I picked went up ten percent!

236
00:09:06,519 --> 00:09:08,440
After deducting taxes and fees,

237
00:09:09,279 --> 00:09:11,320
I made maybe 300,000 or 400,000.

238
00:09:12,519 --> 00:09:13,519
How much?

239
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:15,519
In just that little while,

240
00:09:15,519 --> 00:09:16,480
you made that much money?

241
00:09:17,279 --> 00:09:17,799
So...

242
00:09:18,039 --> 00:09:18,720
is it

243
00:09:19,039 --> 00:09:20,919
transferred to your card or paid in cash?

244
00:09:23,039 --> 00:09:24,399
It's still in the stock market.

245
00:09:24,519 --> 00:09:25,679
Right now it's just numbers,

246
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:26,879
I haven't cashed out yet.

247
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:29,399
You're losing your mind!

248
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,519
No, I can cash it out!

249
00:09:33,919 --> 00:09:35,120
Listen to me, Ma Dawei.

250
00:09:35,399 --> 00:09:37,159
I cooked the ribs and sweet & sour pork.

251
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,240
If you won't eat, Gousheng gets it.

252
00:09:39,639 --> 00:09:40,840
It'll spoil in this heat anyway.

253
00:09:41,279 --> 00:09:41,679
Don't, don't, don't!

254
00:09:41,679 --> 00:09:43,000
Sister-in-law, I'm coming to eat!
